{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKgfY2Zozf1nVgrARLBb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is **PR #6145** (merge commit `e7052745`), titled \"TRUNK-6646: Env-var key normalization drops create_database_* / create_user_* credentials in scripted setup.\" It was merged on 2026-06-12. Its three changed files are all in `openmrs-core`.\n\n**What changed**\n\n1. **Keys kept with underscores.** `normalizeEnvVariableKey` lowercases and turns every `_` into `.` unless the key is in `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS`. So `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME` became `create.database.username`, which the wizard never reads. The fix adds `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME`, `CREATE_DATABASE_PASSWORD`, `CREATE_USER_USERNAME`, `CREATE_USER_PASSWORD` and `CONNECTION_DRIVER_CLASS` to the set, plus several other keys (`IMPORT_TEST_DATA`, `REMOTE_*`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD_LOCKED`).\n2. **Driver alias.** The driver is now read from `connection.driver_class`, falling back to `connection_driver_class`, so both the properties-file and normalized env-var forms work.\n3. **Other script handling.** The same change reads `import_test_data`/`add_demo_data` and `remote_*` values, and it loops over `script` instead of `installScript` when collecting `property.*` entries. It also adds an import-test-data task to the auto-install path.\n4. **Tests.** A new `InitializationFilterNormalizationTest` checks the normalization, and `InitializationFilterTest` gets two tests that feed a fake environment through the wizard initialization.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- I confirmed the dropped-key behaviour from the diff and the normalization code, not by running it. I did not find code in these files that explicitly falls back to root with no password. That part of the symptom is inferred from the missing credentials.\n- Line numbers are from the merge commit. The `InitializationFilterTest` range is approximate.\n- The PR lists TRUNK-5111 as a ticket too, but that appears to 